{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Ccy1SyDjmMXqLuDTCF7t7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've implemented the Mushroom Jump Pad. Here's what I did.\n\n## Investigation\n- The pad (`jumping_pad/jumping_pad.tscn`) is an `Area3D` with a `%mushroom` visual, an (invisible) glowing model, and a box trigger. Its script was an empty `extends Area3D`.\n- The player (`player/player.gd`) is a `CharacterBody3D` that, every physics frame, preserves `velocity.y` and lerps horizontal velocity toward camera-oriented input — so overwriting `velocity` still leaves mid-air steering intact. Gravity is `-30`, jump impulse `12` (+ hold boost), giving a normal max jump of ~2.8 m.\n- The `mushroom.glb` is a single mesh node (cap and stem aren't separable), so squashing the mushroom node's scale reads as a cap bounce (the cap dominates the silhouette).\n- Enemies are `RigidBody3D`, and the three placed pads are only Y-rotated (they launch straight up), but the code handles tilted pads generally.\n\n## Implementation (`jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`)\nMapping to each spec point:\n\n1. **Real physics launch on contact** — `body_entered` overwrites the player's `velocity`, then `move_and_slide` in the player carries it, so ceiling/wall collisions still resolve naturally (no scripted position tween).\n2. **Powerful** — `launch_impulse = 30` → ~15 m rise, far beyond the ~2.8 m normal jump.\n3. **Momentum-independent + retains air control** — velocity is *overwritten* (not added), so incoming speed/direction never carries through; the player's own movement code restores horizontal steering the next frame.\n4. **Launches along surface normal** — direction is `global_transform.basis.y.normalized()`: straight up when flat, up-and-outward on a slope.\n5. **Cap squash + rubbery rebound** — instantly snaps the mushroom to a squashed scale, then tweens back with `TRANS_ELASTIC`/`EASE_OUT`, which overshoots and wobbles past rest before settling; each contact kills the prior tween and restarts.\n6. **Player-only** — `if not body is Player: return`, so enemies/projectiles/etc. pass through with no launch or visual reaction.\n\n## Verification\nRan the project via the Godot MCP: the main scene (with all three pads) loads and the script compiles with **zero errors/warnings**. I stopped the run afterward. Note the MCP can't inject input, so I couldn't drive the character onto a pad in an automated way — the runtime behavior rests on the logic above, which fits the existing player/velocity model.\n\nNo other files were changed — only `jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":36823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":469,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74817858-5a64-4ec6-9fe2-27a540d3f5e5","uuid":"58cb6739-4322-49a5-93c9-b1b129f8ceff","request_id":"req_011Ccy1SwpekRhFEHFgGQgpu"}
